ed_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/json","state":"uploaded","size":653,"digest":"sha256:7ebe8c86abdf505e9a413ba5de5a2a7accdb48f055d9cc8e23540f9e400adfe0","download_count":0,"created_at":"2026-11-18T07:33:16Z","updated_at":"2026-11-18T07:33:16Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/releases/download/m137-v0.13.7/m13stage7-starter-manifest.json"}],"tarball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enginsoysal/engacer-os/tarball/m137-v0.13.7","zipball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enginsoysal/engacer-os/zipball/m137-v0.13.7","body":"# Engacer OS M13.7 / 0.13.7 - Files as the everyday workspace\n\nThis release qualifies the named Files/filter/provider and display tasks within M13-STAGE7-VM-v1. M13.8-M13.12 and final integration remain separate. [Install](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/90d4070b7255c181419d79f0cdfe16ee252319f9/docs/handbook/install-m137.md), [navigate and filter folders](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/90d4070b7255c181419d79f0cdfe16ee252319f9/docs/handbook/files-m137.md), [copy and recover files](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/90d4070b7255c181419d79f0cdfe16ee252319f9/docs/handbook/transfers-m137.md), [decisions](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/90d4070b7255c181419d79f0cdfe16ee252319f9/docs/milestones/m13-7.md).\n\n## Download and verify\n\nExtract the complete VMware ZIP and open EngacerOS.vmx, or use the exact ISO. Keep the supplied devices enabled, blank growable 20-GiB SATA disk, UEFI and Secure Boot off. Choose I Copied It if VMware asks. The package is not preinstalled.\n\n- Build: `a86d9e57c392217a7fe051454180d6df`.\n- ISO SHA256: `51516058e73d0353c18e4fb8e1340d06d5655235e8e3eb40e7824c335c071dae`.\n- VMware ZIP SHA256: `d251f5071d129d51678ca567160e6456c0943c8d330121993ec385a3c9084cc6`.\n\nTwenty assets include media, maps, exact build/starter manifests, checksums, notices and applicable third-party source/licenses. The frozen native build binds 608 compiled inputs.\n\n## What changes\n\nFiles has a compact common navigation/command frame, original place icons, a quiet 192-unit sidebar, clear page arrows and concise item/selection status. Small windows expose Places and More instead of overlapping controls. Breadcrumbs/address editing, details/icons, ordering, provider history and real file operations remain available. A single native folder opens in the same Files window through Enter/context Open, matching ordinary mouse navigation and preserving Back/Forward; desktop and explicit new-window launches remain separate.\n\nCtrl+F opens a bounded current-folder name filter. Case-insensitive displayed-name substring matching accepts up to 63 ASCII query bytes; it adds no background index, heap cache or process per keystroke. Each live window generation owns its query. Query changes clear hidden selection and scroll offset. Enter selects the first result without opening it; Escape clears the query before leaving the field. Clear/navigation/reuse and successful create/copy/move transitions are explicit; Refresh/sorting retain the same-folder query. Recycle Bin uses original displayed names and requires clearing a filter before Empty Bin.\n\nUSB filtering remains explicitly unavailable. Real supported USB navigation, long addresses, lease-bound detach/replacement, transfers and Eject retain provider/capability ownership. Eject follows the existing flush-before-removal path. Unsupported formats/search/hardware are not implied by the visual changes.\n\n## Exact native qualification\n\n75 named native task/profile checks bind the media: five complete Files display journeys, shared controls/gallery tasks, actual applied Files themes, current-folder queries, selection, same-window history, modal/new-window ownership, create/copy/move results, real USB provider/import/long-address/replacement/safe removal, transfer/cancel/conflict tasks and independent disk starts. The exact enabled-device VMware starter installs, restarts with ISO retained and starts twice without ISO. See [acceptance](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/90d4070b7255c181419d79f0cdfe16ee252319f9/evidence/M13/7/acceptance-results.json), [resource record](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/90d4070b7255c181419d79f0cdfe16ee252319f9/evidence/M13/7/resources.json) and [visual review](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/90d4070b7255c181419d79f0cdfe16ee252319f9/evidence/M13/7/visual-review.json).\n\nFixed desktop state is 554,140 bytes, +704 bytes for eight bounded filter records. Fixed installer state remains 48,412 bytes; font masks remain 251,248 bytes. Completed named tasks retain zero managed pages and idle CPUs halt. Configured RAM, physical framebuffer bytes and managed current/peak/retained memory are separate. Feedback/frame timing remains M13.9.\n\nThe earlier stale-empty-cache and Enter/new-window observations remain diagnostic failures on earlier unqualified candidates. Their corrected final-media tasks are separately repeated; old or cancelled checks never qualify these bytes.\n\n## Scope and limits\n\nThis is current native system-folder ASCII name filtering, not recursive/content or USB search. Named VM tasks do not establish a fresh fourteen-controller matrix, universal physical hardware, vendor GPU 3D or general Windows/DOS compatibility. Agent scenario/visual review is separate from an actual human novice study. Matching GitHub downloads and complete public website closure are separate gates.\n"}